{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"ps2-controller","name":"PS2 wireless controller","version":"1.0.1","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"The PS2-style wireless game pad that comes with most robot car kits: its receiver goes on the board (PS2X_lib.h), the pad's buttons and sticks drive the robot. Play it with a real game pad plugged into your PC, the keyboard (arrows, 1-4, Q/E, Enter), or the run panel.","category":"Controls","needsApp":"0.9.0","code":"// A PS2 wireless pad's receiver. The board asks with a message on ATT ([0x42, ...]); it answers on DAT\n// with the pad's real data bytes: buttons (two bytes, a bit each, 0 = pressed), then the sticks RX, RY,\n// LX, LY (0..255, 128 in the middle).\nconst BITS = { Select: 0x0001, L3: 0x0002, R3: 0x0004, Start: 0x0008, Up: 0x0010, Right: 0x0020, Down: 0x0040, Left: 0x0080, L2: 0x0100, R2: 0x0200, L1: 0x0400, R1: 0x0800, Triangle: 0x1000, Circle: 0x2000, Cross: 0x4000, Square: 0x8000 };\nbench.device('ps2', (part) => {\n  const on = part.control('on'), keys = part.control('buttons');\n  const lx = part.control('lx'), ly = part.control('ly'), rx = part.control('rx'), ry = part.control('ry');\n  const led = part.screen('led');\n  let powered = false, asks = 0, pending = 0, held = '';\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      powered = io.supply('VCC', 'GND') >= 2.8;\n      const linked = powered && on.on;\n      led.set(0, 0, linked ? 1 : 0);\n      if (pending && linked) {\n        let b = 0;\n        const down = keys.down;\n        for (const k of down) b |= BITS[k] ?? 0;\n        held = [...down].join(' ');\n        const lo = ~b & 255, hi = (~b >> 8) & 255;\n        for (let i = 0; i < pending; i++) io.send('DAT', 'data', [lo, hi, rx.value | 0, ry.value | 0, lx.value | 0, ly.value | 0]);\n      }\n      pending = 0;\n      io.draw(powered ? 0.02 : 0);\n    },\n    packets(list) {\n      for (const p of list) if (p.pin === 'ATT' && p.proto === 'data' && p.data[0] === 0x42) { pending = Math.min(4, pending + 1); asks++; }\n    },\n    status: () => [!powered ? 'no power' : !on.on ? 'pad switched off (no answer)' : `pad linked${held ? `: ${held}` : ''}`, `sticks L ${lx.value | 0},${ly.value | 0} R ${rx.value | 0},${ry.value | 0}`, `${asks} reads`],\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"PS2X_lib.h":{"classes":["PS2X"],"exports":["PSB_SELECT","PSB_L3","PSB_R3","PSB_START","PSB_PAD_UP","PSB_PAD_RIGHT","PSB_PAD_DOWN","PSB_PAD_LEFT","PSB_L2","PSB_R2","PSB_L1","PSB_R1","PSB_GREEN","PSB_RED","PSB_BLUE","PSB_PINK","PSB_TRIANGLE","PSB_CIRCLE","PSB_CROSS","PSB_SQUARE","PSS_RX","PSS_RY","PSS_LX","PSS_LY","PSAB_PAD_RIGHT","PSAB_PAD_UP","PSAB_PAD_DOWN","PSAB_PAD_LEFT","PSAB_L2","PSAB_R2","PSAB_L1","PSAB_R1","PSAB_GREEN","PSAB_RED","PSAB_BLUE","PSAB_PINK","PSAB_TRIANGLE","PSAB_CIRCLE","PSAB_CROSS","PSAB_SQUARE"],"code":"// PS2X_lib.h (Bill Porter's library), the parts most sketches use:\n//   PS2X ps2x;  int error = ps2x.config_gamepad(CLK, CMD, ATT, DAT, false, false);  (0 = found)\n//   loop: ps2x.read_gamepad(false, 0);\n//         ps2x.Button(PSB_PAD_UP) (held), ps2x.ButtonPressed(PSB_CROSS) (just now), ButtonReleased, NewButtonState()\n//         ps2x.Analog(PSS_LY) (0..255, 128 in the middle; up is 0)\n//   ps2x.readType() (1: a DualShock)\n// (It asks the receiver with a message on ATT and reads its answer on DAT.)\nconst PSB_SELECT = 0x0001, PSB_L3 = 0x0002, PSB_R3 = 0x0004, PSB_START = 0x0008, PSB_PAD_UP = 0x0010, PSB_PAD_RIGHT = 0x0020, PSB_PAD_DOWN = 0x0040, PSB_PAD_LEFT = 0x0080;\nconst PSB_L2 = 0x0100, PSB_R2 = 0x0200, PSB_L1 = 0x0400, PSB_R1 = 0x0800, PSB_GREEN = 0x1000, PSB_RED = 0x2000, PSB_BLUE = 0x4000, PSB_PINK = 0x8000;\nconst PSB_TRIANGLE = 0x1000, PSB_CIRCLE = 0x2000, PSB_CROSS = 0x4000, PSB_SQUARE = 0x8000;\nconst PSS_RX = 5, PSS_RY = 6, PSS_LX = 7, PSS_LY = 8;\nconst PSAB_PAD_RIGHT = 9, PSAB_PAD_UP = 11, PSAB_PAD_DOWN = 12, PSAB_PAD_LEFT = 10, PSAB_L2 = 19, PSAB_R2 = 20, PSAB_L1 = 17, PSAB_R1 = 18;\nconst PSAB_GREEN = 13, PSAB_RED = 14, PSAB_BLUE = 15, PSAB_PINK = 16, PSAB_TRIANGLE = 13, PSAB_CIRCLE = 14, PSAB_CROSS = 15, PSAB_SQUARE = 16;\nclass PS2X {\n  constructor() { this.att = -1; this.dat = -1; this.buttons = 0xffff; this.last = 0xffff; this.data = [0xff, 0xff, 128, 128, 128, 128]; this.found = false; }\n  _ask() {\n    linkReceive(this.dat, 'data'); // (nothing stale)\n    linkSend(this.att, 'data', [0x42, 0, 0]);\n    const t = millis();\n    while (millis() - t < 30) {\n      const got = linkReceive(this.dat, 'data');\n      if (got.length) return got[got.length - 1].data;\n      delay(1);\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n  config_gamepad(clk, cmd, att, dat, pressures = false, rumble = false) {\n    this.att = att; this.dat = dat;\n    pinMode(clk, OUTPUT); pinMode(cmd, OUTPUT); pinMode(att, OUTPUT); pinMode(dat, INPUT);\n    digitalWrite(att, HIGH);\n    for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) { if (this._ask()) { this.found = true; return 0; } delay(10); }\n    return 1; // (no controller found: wiring, power, or the pad is off)\n  }\n  read_gamepad(motor1 = false, motor2 = 0) {\n    if (this.att < 0) return false;\n    const d = this._ask();\n    this.last = this.buttons;\n    if (!d) return false;\n    this.data = d;\n    this.buttons = d[0] | (d[1] << 8);\n    return true;\n  }\n  readType() { return this.found ? 1 : 0; }\n  Button(b) { return (~this.buttons & b) > 0; }\n  ButtonPressed(b) { return this.NewButtonState(b) && this.Button(b); }\n  ButtonReleased(b) { return this.NewButtonState(b) && (~this.last & b) > 0; }\n  NewButtonState(b) { return b === undefined ? (this.last ^ this.buttons) > 0 : ((this.last ^ this.buttons) & b) > 0; }\n  ButtonDataByte() { return ~this.buttons & 0xffff; }\n  Analog(i) {\n    if (i >= 5 && i <= 8) return this.data[i - 3]; // RX RY LX LY\n    return this.Button(1 << ((i - 9) & 15)) ? 255 : 0; // (pressure: full, as with pressures off)\n  }\n  enableRumble() {} enablePressures() { return false; } reconfig_gamepad() {}\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"ps2-receiver","name":"PS2 controller receiver","description":"The wireless pad's receiver: wire DAT, CMD, ATT (also called CS / SEL) and CLK to four pins, VCC to 3.3 V (5 V on many boards' receivers works too) and GND. With #include <PS2X_lib.h>: PS2X ps2x; ps2x.config_gamepad(CLK, CMD, ATT, DAT, false, false) == 0 when it finds the pad; in loop(): ps2x.read_gamepad(); ps2x.Button(PSB_PAD_UP), ps2x.ButtonPressed(PSB_CROSS), ps2x.Analog(PSS_LY) (0 up .. 128 middle .. 255 down). The pad: a game pad on your PC, the keyboard (arrows = D-pad, 1-4 = triangle circle cross square, Q / E = L1 / R1, Enter = Start), or the run panel.","swatch":"#1a1a1c","mass":8,"shape":[{"box":[5,1.3,4.7],"at":[0,0.65,0],"color":"#1a1a1c"},{"screen":{"id":"led","size":[0.3,0.3],"px":[1,1],"mode":"pixels","on":"#30d158","off":"#123018","bg":"#1a1a1c"},"at":[1.4,1.31,1.3]}],"pins":[{"id":"DAT","label":"DAT (data from the pad)","at":[-1.3,0.3,-2.4],"kind":"out"},{"id":"CMD","label":"CMD (commands to it)","at":[-0.9,0.3,-2.4],"kind":"in"},{"id":"VCC","label":"VCC (3.3 V)","at":[-0.5,0.3,-2.4],"kind":"vin","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5},{"id":"GND","at":[-0.1,0.3,-2.4],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"ATT","label":"ATT (CS / SEL)","at":[0.3,0.3,-2.4],"kind":"in"},{"id":"CLK","label":"CLK","at":[0.7,0.3,-2.4],"kind":"in"}],"controls":[{"id":"on","kind":"switch","label":"Pad switched on","value":true},{"id":"buttons","kind":"keys","label":"Buttons","cols":4,"keys":["Up","Down","Left","Right","Triangle","Circle","Cross","Square","L1","R1","L2","R2","Start","Select","L3","R3"]},{"id":"lx","kind":"slider","label":"Left stick left-right","min":0,"max":255,"step":1,"value":128},{"id":"ly","kind":"slider","label":"Left stick up-down","min":0,"max":255,"step":1,"value":128},{"id":"rx","kind":"slider","label":"Right stick left-right","min":0,"max":255,"step":1,"value":128},{"id":"ry","kind":"slider","label":"Right stick up-down","min":0,"max":255,"step":1,"value":128}],"device":"ps2"}],"examples":[]}